    "body": "Agreed on resetting `[[state]]` to \"closed\" on error.\n\nIn practice, `open` often fails on Linux due to file permissions on the hidraw device node. I think Android has similar behavior if the user denies access in the system-level device permission prompt. This can also fail on Windows when trying to access a device that is already exclusively claimed by a platform driver ([some HID devices](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/hid/hid-architecture#hid-clients-supported-in-windows) are not available for shared access on Windows).",
